        "parms": "# ~sine — a pure tone\nA ~sine is an oscillator that plays a sine wave, the purest tone: one frequency and nothing above it. Its argument is the frequency in Hz, 440 by default. A float on its inlet sets the frequency; a signal there modulates it (FM).\nMax's cycle~ also reads a wavetable and has a phase inlet; ~sine has neither. On the engine Phi ships its inlet takes floats only: an int, from a message box 440 or an i box, is ignored. Write 440. or use an f box.",
